BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wyxr-event-603bc1ca-df0e-4f8c-9afa-510b8c6a9953@concert-calendar.wyxr.o
 rg
DTSTAMP:20261007T113656Z
DTSTART:20261019T230000Z
DTEND:20261020T020000Z
SUMMARY:Memphis Drone (12+ artists) — H and S Printing Company
LOCATION:H and S Printing Company\, Memphis\, TN
DESCRIPTION:Show 6 PM\nNASHVILLE\, TN – September 22\, 2026 – chatterbi
 rd\, a Nashville-based chamber ensemble\, is excited to partner with Memph
 is Print Shop and numerous Memphis-based artists for Memphis Drone\, a six
 -hour concert of uninterrupted sound. The concert takes place at Memphis P
 rint Shop on Monday\, October 19\, from 6:00 PM until midnight. Memphis Dr
 one is co-produced by Jenny Davis\, Robert Traxler\, Unmanageable Arts\, H
 yasynth House\, and Gezellig Records. Tickets are on sale now and can be p
 urchased here.\n \nMemphis Drone is part of three durational drone concert
 s across Tennessee\, with the other two taking place at future dates and l
 ocations later this fall. Each six-hour concert featuring over twelve musi
 cians performing interlocking\, collaborative sets will transform communit
 ies into temporary creative ecosystems where musicians\, visual artists\, 
 and audiences explore sustained sound and shifting tones over time.\n \nFe
 atured performers for Memphis Drone include chatterbird\, Dwight Van de Va
 te\, Eudamonia Flue Quartet\, Eve Maret\, Infinity Stairs\, Madame Fraanki
 e\, Marcella Simien\, Optic Sink\, Robby Grant\, Sean Murphy\, Tamar Love\
 , and Thomas Corbin.\n \nDesigned as miniature community festivals\, these
  experimental durational concerts\, often called “drones”\, prioritize
  deep listening\, presence\, improvisation\, collaboration\, and collectiv
 e participation. Defined by sustained tones and repetition\, drone is one 
 of the world’s oldest musical forms\, resonating across cultures from In
 digenous Australian didgeridoos and Indian tanpuras to Scottish bagpipes a
 nd Tibetan Buddhist chant. By centering this universal musical structure\,
  the project creates an accessible framework for participation while uplif
 ting artists who work outside commercial music systems.\n \nABOUT THE PROD
 UCERS:\nJENNY DAVIS is a Memphis-based musician\, arts administrator\, and
  community arts organizer. A flutist by training\, she has worked across p
 erformance\, music education\, and nonprofit arts leadership. She is inter
 ested in creating collaborative\, accessible arts experiences that bring t
 ogether artists\, organizations\, and audiences through experiences that e
 ncourage connection\, curiosity\, and collaboration.\n\nROBERT TRAXLER sta
 rted the Memphis Concrète experimental electronic music festival in 2017.
  He sometimes makes his own music.\n\nCHATTERBIRD is a chamber music ensem
 ble that explores alternative instrumentation\, stylistic diversity\, and 
 interdisciplinary collaboration in order to create thoughtful\, intimate\,
  and inventive musical experiences. Formed in 2014\, chatterbird performs 
 classical music that skirts traditional boundaries\, sliding between class
 ical\, jazz\, hip-hop\, rock\, avant-garde\, and country\, creating a thou
 ghtful and inventive way to discover and experience modern classical music
 .\n\nHYASYNTH HOUSE was founded in 2018 and is a Nashville-based electroni
 c music collective that serves to empower female and LQBTQIA+ artists in t
 he community through the curation of public workshops\, showcases\, and li
 ve music performances. IG: @hyasynth_house\n\nGEZELLIG ARTS is the live ev
 ent services branch of Gezellig Records\, an internationally-minded/Knoxvi
 lle-based independent record label run by Ben Smith\, who also organized t
 he 12-Hour Drone events as part of the 2018 + 2019 editions of the Big Ear
 s Festival.\n\nUNMANAGEABLE ARTS is a 501c3 non-profit whose mission is to
  mobilize resources and build power for artists engaged in social change w
 ork. We support artist-driven projects that connect across history\, cultu
 re\, and communities\, and prioritize projects that are anti-racist and ro
 oted in feminist ideology.\nhttps://concert-calendar.wyxr.org/e/603bc1ca-d
 f0e-4f8c-9afa-510b8c6a9953
URL:https://concert-calendar.wyxr.org/e/603bc1ca-df0e-4f8c-9afa-510b8c6a995
 3
CATEGORIES:WYXR Pick
LAST-MODIFIED:20261007T113722Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
